# Running the Researcher

## Quick Commands

### Single Run (Production)
```bash
cd researcher
go run . --once
```

### Local Mode (No GitHub Push)
```bash
go run . --once --repo-path "../gitopedia" --no-commit
```

### Step-by-Step Mode
```bash
# Auto-advance through steps
go run . --once --step --repo-path "../gitopedia" --no-commit

# Run specific step
go run . --once --step --step-name discovery --repo-path "../gitopedia" --no-commit
```

### Continuous Loop
```bash
go run .  # Runs forever, checks every 60s
```

### Merge-Only Mode
```bash
go run . --merge-only  # Only merge ready PRs
```

## Available Steps
- `discovery` - Search web for sources
- `summarization` - Summarize first relevant source  
- `drafting` - Generate article from summary
- `finalize` - Create PR (skipped in local mode)

## CLI Flags
| Flag | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `--once` | Run one iteration and exit |
| `--step` | Step-by-step mode with pauses |
| `--step-name` | Specific step to run |
| `--repo-path` | Path to local gitopedia repo |
| `--no-commit` | Stage changes but don't commit |
| `--merge-only` | Only merge ready PRs |
